Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: apps/lib/cmp_mock_srv.c
Line: 593
Function: process_genm
Bug type: use-after-free
CWE: CWE-416
Explanation: On the error path when handling a single ITAV (rsp == NULL or push fails), the code frees *out with sk_OSSL_CMP_ITAV_free(*out) but does not set *out to NULL before returning 0. This leaves a dangling pointer visible to the caller. If the caller attempts cleanup by using or freeing *out after the function returns failure, it can lead to use-after-free or double free. This path is reachable if process_genm_itav() returns NULL or if sk_OSSL_CMP_ITAV_push() fails (e.g., under memory pressure).

Source context:
